.venv/
_meta/.cache/
__pycache__/
# The embeddings artifact is MOUNTED, not copied: docker-compose.yml bind-mounts
# /home/dzinck/mcp-assets/embeddings over /repo/_meta/embeddings read-only. Excluding it here
# keeps 253 MiB of vectors out of the image and out of the registry, and lets the artifact be
# replaced without a rebuild. (An earlier version of this comment said numpy was absent and
# the vectors were unreadable dead weight — that stopped being true when serve-time semantic
# search was enabled; requirements.txt now installs torch + sentence-transformers.)
_meta/embeddings/
# 1.04 GiB, and NOT read at runtime. Snapshots are the provenance evidence for
# corpus-verify-provenance; grep confirms zero references to them anywhere under
# corpus_toolkit/mcp/ — every consumer is in validate/provenance.py or grounding.py, both
# CLI/CI. Shipping them made the image 25% larger for a file the server never opens.
#
# Consequence, stated so it is not a surprise: `corpus-verify-provenance` cannot run INSIDE
# the container. It is a CI gate and belongs there; run it against a checkout, not an image.
_meta/snapshots/
# Generated at deploy time by the pages workflow; never needed at runtime.
site/
# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored — it is a RUNTIME dependency (the FTS cache key is
# `git rev-parse HEAD` + a hash of `git status --porcelain`, and corpus_overview() runs
# `git log -1`). Build from a depth-1 clone to keep it small; see the Dockerfile header.
#
# Measured caveat on that "keep it small": depth-1 elides HISTORY, but one commit of a repo
# this size still needs every blob in its tree, so /repo/.git is ~495 MB in the built image,
# not the ~20 MB the Dockerfile header implies. Removing it entirely needs a generated
# build-info.json in the toolkit (corpus-toolkit's own issue), not a change here.
